          <MultilingualText ID="E" CompositionName="Comment">
            <ObjectList>
              <MultilingualTextItem ID="F" CompositionName="Items">
                <AttributeList>
                  <Culture>en-US</Culture>
                  <Text>Banks cumulative high-and-running time across plant-stop pauses (NEW-HBA-01), replacing the former countdown budget (F1/F2/S1 fix, 2026-07-20). AccumulatedElapsed has two provably-disjoint writers, so there is no same-scan race and no next-scan cleanup (the F2/S1 root cause is gone): it is reset to T#0S on a genuine confirmed clear (NOT HighQualified) or on FaultReset, and otherwise banked up by the just-ended segment's elapsed only on a real plant-stop pause (PauseEdge AND HighQualified AND NOT FaultReset - i.e. the hopper is still blocked but the plant stopped). PauseEdge is a constructed falling edge (C-404); it and the bank read PersistenceTimer.ET from before NETWORK 4's TON re-evaluates this scan, so the ET captured is the just-completed segment's, with no separate held-value register needed.</Text>
                </AttributeList>
              </MultilingualTextItem>
            </ObjectList>
          </MultilingualText>
          <MultilingualText ID="10" CompositionName="Title">
            <ObjectList>
