            <ObjectList>
              <MultilingualTextItem ID="19" CompositionName="Items">
                <AttributeList>
                  <Culture>en-US</Culture>
                  <Text>Latched fault (C-123): set when cumulative high-and-running time reaches BlockedTimeThreshold (CumulativeElapsed >= threshold), held until FaultReset. FaultReset gates the whole rung (AND NOT FaultReset) so a reset clears the latch regardless of the trip's current state (F1 fix - the old rung let a still-true trip defeat the reset); paired with NETWORK 3/4 zeroing the accumulator and current segment, a reset requires a fresh full accumulation before re-alarming, identically whether the trip was contiguous or post-pause. Lives in the RETAIN interface and deliberately survives a power cycle (C-124 carve-out, NEW-HBA-04) - a blockage needing a human still needs acknowledgement after a restart, like the sequencer's DischargeConveyorTimeoutFault. Fail-safe: the stop demand below stays asserted until acknowledged.</Text>
                </AttributeList>
              </MultilingualTextItem>
            </ObjectList>
          </MultilingualText>
